From d5340ad9b10cea49485b57d2cbedbca188f1f9b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 18:29:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add an aperture control

A camera with a controllable aperture gets a button in the controls bar,
next to focus. What the popover offers depends on the hardware:

* A lens with fixed stops, such as the two-position blade mechanism on a
  Galaxy S9, gets one linked toggle per stop, labelled f/1.5 and f/2.4.
  A slider would imply values the mechanism cannot reach.
* A continuously variable iris gets a slider marked with its extremes,
  throttled the same way the focus slider is.

A camera with a fixed aperture advertises no LensAperture control and so
gets no button.

The aperture library learns to report the values of an enumeration whose
entries have no names. PipeWire sends labels only for controls whose
values are named, such as a list of modes, so a control enumerating plain
numbers arrived with an empty choice list even though those numbers were
the only values it would accept. Its bounds are now the extremes of the
enumerated set rather than its first two entries, which was only right by
accident for a set of two.

Signed-off-by: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
